 "text": "Someone's making fun of you? Don't fight back. Do this. Therapists call it fogging. It comes from a 1975 book, \"When I Say No, I Feel Guilty.\" Here's the trick. Calmly agree with any part that's true. \"Nice shoes, Grandpa.\" \"Yeah, they're comfy.\" \"You're always late.\" \"True, I was late today.\" No anger, no defending. Like fog, they throw punches and nothing lands. Why it works? A tease wants a reaction. Give it nothing and it has nothing to grab. One thing. This is for teasing. If it's bullying or it keeps happening, tell someone you trust. Follow for more mind tricks.",
